\[ F(n) = \begin{cases} 
  0 & \text{if } n = 0 \\
  1 & \text{if } n = 1 \\
  F(n-1) + F(n-2) & \text{if } n > 1 
\end{cases} \]

Given \( F(0) = 2 \) and \( F(1) = 4 \), let's calculate the next few terms using this recursive method to identify a pattern or to get to the next number in the sequence.

